/E (Grief in Relationships: \(Loss, Disappointment, Change\) Relationships die slowly. People change, needs diverge, the relationship you had isn't the relationship you need anymore. Healthy couples grieve these micro-deaths and renegotiate. When you can't grieve and renegotiate, the relationship becomes a corpse you're still maintaining. Real love sometimes means releasing someone.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [1]
>>
