/P 497 0 R
/E (Commitment & Covenant: The choice to stay when it gets hard. Not just romantic marriage \(though that's one form\), but the decision to keep showing up despite disconnection, boredom, or difficulty. This is different from obligation or fear-based staying. Real commitment is choosing someone not because you have to, but because they matter more than your comfort.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [2]
