/E (Nervous System Co-Regulation: \(Borrowing Calm\) When you're dysregulated and someone with a calm nervous system sits with you, their calmness can transfer to you. Your heart rate synchronizes with theirs. Your breathing pattern mirrors theirs. This is why being near a safe person can literally change your physiology. This is why isolation during stress is so damaging.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1659 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 497 0 R
/E (Emotional Contagion: \(Moods Spread Like Viruses\) You walk into a room and immediately pick up the vibe. One person's anxiety can spread to the whole group; one person's joy can lift everyone. This happens through mirror neurons, through pheromones, through subtle cues you're not consciously aware of. This is why toxic people drain rooms and secure people calm them.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
