/E (Phenomenological Presence: \(Radical Attention\) To be truly present is to set aside your agenda and fully meet someone. Not waiting for your turn to talk, not planning your response, not thinking about what you'll do after. True presence is a suspension of self for the sake of meeting the other. It's rare, difficult, and transformative.)
/Pg 50 0 R
