/E (Existential Responsibility to the Other \(Levinas\): The philosopher Emmanuel Levinas suggested that the other person's face creates an ethical obligation that precedes all calculation. Simply by existing, they place a claim on you: care for me, don't harm me, be responsible to my vulnerability. This isn't warm and fuzzy; it's a duty embedded in meeting another human.)
/Pg 50 0 R
