/E (The Violence of Not Being Seen: In psychological research and literature, one of the deepest harms is chronic invisibility. When someone's inner experience is repeatedly invalidated or ignored, it creates existential erasure. Children who aren't mirrored often develop dissociation or profound shame. Adults who aren't seen in their relationships develop a quiet kind of death. Being seen is not luxury; it's necessity.)
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [5]
>>
